The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
if (fc->writeback_cache)
	mapping_set_writeback_may_deadlock_on_reclaim(&inode->i_data);
```
Reason: This line does not set `AS_NO_DATA_INTEGRITY` on the mapping. As a result, `wait_sb_inodes()` does not skip fuse inodes with writeback cache and waits for all writeback to complete, causing a hang if the fuse server is faulty.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
if (fc->writeback_cache) {
	mapping_set_writeback_may_deadlock_on_reclaim(&inode->i_data);
	mapping_set_no_data_integrity(&inode->i_data);
}
```
Reason: Adding `mapping_set_no_data_integrity()` marks the mapping as not requiring data integrity guarantees, so `wait_sb_inodes()` skips these inodes and avoids waiting for writeback to complete on an unresponsive server.

